1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,065
This is Strike: weekly options vaults
for Robinhood Chain stock tokens.

2
00:00:05,115 --> 00:00:07,636
A covered call pays a weekly premium,

3
00:00:07,686 --> 00:00:09,926
but someone has to pick the strike.

4
00:00:09,976 --> 00:00:12,155
Here an AI agent picks it,

5
00:00:12,205 --> 00:00:15,158
and the contract checks
it against a mandate.

6
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:19,414
The playground asks the deployed
Epoch Manager about a proposal,

7
00:00:19,464 --> 00:00:20,702
with no wallet.

8
00:00:20,752 --> 00:00:24,347
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

9
00:00:24,397 --> 00:00:26,464
A reckless at-the-money strike:

10
00:00:26,514 --> 00:00:28,867
rejected, delta out of band.

11
00:00:28,917 --> 00:00:33,363
A real one would cost the
agent 10 USDG of its bond.

12
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:36,429
It happened for real on September 29.

13
00:00:36,479 --> 00:00:40,611
The seller agent asked for
a 0.20-delta Tesla call,

14
00:00:40,661 --> 00:00:47,178
and the contract solved the strike
on-chain: $369.86, accepted.

15
00:00:47,228 --> 00:00:50,361
Then a reckless agent
forced an at-the-money put.

16
00:00:50,411 --> 00:00:53,263
Rejected, and 10 USDG slashed:

17
00:00:53,313 --> 00:00:55,924
its bond went from 60 to 50.

18
00:00:55,974 --> 00:00:59,015
Here it is on the
Robinhood Chain explorer.

19
00:00:59,065 --> 00:01:03,418
The status says Success, because
a rejection is not a revert.

20
00:01:03,468 --> 00:01:06,981
The transaction ran, the
contract refused the proposal,

21
00:01:07,031 --> 00:01:10,687
and 10 USDG left the agent's bond.

22
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:12,991
The Tesla covered-call vault this week:

23
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:17,553
the $369.86 call, all four sold

24
00:01:17,603 --> 00:01:21,031
to a buyer agent, for 10.01 USDG.

25
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:25,452
The buyer profits above $372.36.

26
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:29,743
At or below the strike,
depositors keep the whole premium.

27
00:01:29,793 --> 00:01:32,517
A risk engine written in Rust on Stylus

28
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:35,095
stress-tests this week's option on-chain.

29
00:01:35,145 --> 00:01:38,466
Its worst case: a 30% jump in Tesla,

30
00:01:38,516 --> 00:01:42,492
and −$321.40 for the vault.

31
00:01:42,542 --> 00:01:46,964
Agent one is ERC-8004 identity 114:

32
00:01:47,014 --> 00:01:51,628
one accepted, one rejected,
and a 50 USDG bond.

33
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:54,033
This monitor reads every stock token

34
00:01:54,083 --> 00:01:56,543
on Robinhood Chain mainnet, live.

35
00:01:56,593 --> 00:02:02,370
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

36
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:05,071
so Strike never applies it twice.

37
00:02:05,121 --> 00:02:08,906
Over 403 weekly epochs since 2019,

38
00:02:08,956 --> 00:02:14,359
the covered call traded upside
for 25 to 46% lower volatility.

39
00:02:14,409 --> 00:02:20,252
On Nvidia, from 45.6% down to 26.5%.

40
00:02:20,302 --> 00:02:22,892
891 tests and proofs,

41
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,740
99.3% line coverage,

42
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:28,164
nine properties proven with Halmos,

43
00:02:28,214 --> 00:02:30,858
all 11 internal-review findings fixed,

44
00:02:30,908 --> 00:02:35,860
and a Stylus strike solver
that uses 6.5 times less gas.

45
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:38,324
Strike: options on Robinhood Chain,

46
00:02:38,374 --> 00:02:41,425
run by agents the contract
holds to a mandate.

47
00:02:41,475 --> 00:02:45,943
Try the playground at
strike-options.vercel.app.

48
00:02:45,993 --> 00:02:48,883
It is unaudited, and on testnet.
